-- Staff (Session 7). Real auth.users + auth.identities rows, in the same
-- shape a genuine supabase.auth.signUp() produces (verified by doing one
-- against the local instance and inspecting the result) — not a shortcut
-- shape that happens to satisfy the staff FK but couldn't actually log in.
-- The on_auth_user_created trigger fires off each insert below and creates
-- the matching public.staff row itself (name from raw_user_meta_data, role
-- defaulted); the UPDATE afterward assigns the specific roster this app's
-- dummy data has always used, regardless of insertion-order bootstrap
-- quirks. Password for all four, local dev only: "password123".
-- confirmation_token/recovery_token/email_change_token_new/email_change have
-- no column default (plain NULL) but GoTrue's Go code scans them as
-- non-nullable strings — a real signup or admin-create call always leaves
-- them as '', never NULL. Omitting them here is what actually broke sign-in
-- the first time this seed was written: "converting NULL to string is
-- unsupported" from the /token endpoint. Set explicitly so these rows are
-- byte-for-byte what a genuine signup produces, not a shape that merely
-- satisfies the staff FK.
   raw_app_meta_data, raw_user_meta_data, created_at, updated_at,
   confirmation_token, recovery_token, email_change_token_new, email_change)
