-- Chart of Accounts (Session 12, plus Session 14's and Session 19's later
-- additions) used to be seeded here — moved into
-- 20260819090000_seed_gap_accounts_expense_categories.sql instead, once a
-- full seed-vs-migration audit found accounts had never been in a
-- migration at all, meaning production (which never runs this file) had
-- zero rows in it and every auto-posting call was failing. That migration
-- now inserts all 41 accounts unconditionally (accounts has no branch or
-- staff dependency once accounts.created_by is nullable, so it's safe to
-- run before this file ever does), so re-inserting the same 41 rows here
-- would just hit accounts_code_key's unique constraint. See that
-- migration for the real content and reasoning; nothing else in this file
-- depends on exactly where in the seed sequence accounts gets populated,
-- since it's now already fully populated before this file even starts.

-- expense_category_accounts: maps every category in the seeded
-- expense_categories list (Session 4) to a real GL account, so
-- post_expense_journal_entry() has somewhere to post each one. "Staff
-- advances" deliberately maps to 1350 Advances to Staff (an asset, not an
-- expense account) — see the Session 14 migration header's "one loop
-- closed" note. Every category not listed here (including any a Manager
-- adds later through Settings) falls back to 5900 Miscellaneous Expense at
-- posting time via expense_category_account()'s own default, so this list
-- doesn't need to be exhaustive.
select '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', category, (select id from public.accounts where code = code_value)
from (values
  ('Transport', '5120'),
  ('Fuel', '5130'),
  ('Rent', '5100'),
  ('Utilities', '5110'),
  ('Casual labour', '5150'),
  ('Repairs & maintenance', '5160'),
  ('Supplies', '5170'),
  ('Staff advances', '1350'),
  ('Miscellaneous', '5900')
) as mapping(category, code_value);

-- bank_accounts (Session 16, reworked by the multi-bank-account posting
-- migration): four real bank accounts, each tied to its OWN dedicated,
-- postable Assets sub-account (1011–1014) rather than all sharing the
-- 1010 Cash in Bank rollup — 1010 is non-postable as of that migration.
-- The dedicated sub-accounts must exist before the bank_accounts rows
-- that link to them (validate_bank_account_gl_link rejects a link to
-- 1010, a non-postable account, or a missing one). On production the same
-- split is done by repointing the existing bank account(s) in the
-- migration itself; this file only ever runs locally, so it provisions
-- the whole set directly. opening_balance is each real bank's own balance
-- as of the stated date, independent of the ledger's own running balance
-- (no opening-balance entries exist yet — the gap Session 15 flagged).
on conflict (code) do nothing;


